{
  "_comment": "Canonical cross-runtime crash:v1 test vectors. Reproducible by any runtime (native Rust, wasm, TS) from the pinned algorithm documented in libs/games/src/crash/v1/math.rs. All values are integer/ppm; no floating point.",
  "algorithm": {
    "game_type": "crash:v1",
    "derivation": "v1",
    "seed_derivation": "digest(decision, chunk) = blake2b-256 of b'99dot5:engine-seed:v1' (21 bytes, no terminator) || u8 len(game_type) || game_type || u8 len(server_seed) || server_seed || u8 len(client_seed) || client_seed || decision u32 LE || chunk u32 LE. The three text fields are their ASCII bytes as fed to the engine (the 64-hex strings in production) and may not exceed 255 bytes. A decision's randomness is read sequentially from chunk 0, 32 bytes per chunk, at most 4 chunks (128 bytes). preimage_example_hex is the preimage for game_type 'hilo:v1', server_seed '11'*32, client_seed '22'*32, decision 3, chunk 1. crash:v1: the bet is decision 0; raw_u64 = little-endian u64 of stream bytes [0..8]. The cashout and the expire draw nothing",
    "preimage_example_hex": "",
    "preimage_example_digest_hex": "e032790ea31b22d5299594aa1de0d461e67cc3b398d5aec5d4685d98684599db",
    "house_edge_ppm": 995000,
    "scale_ppm": 1000000,
    "max_multiplier_cap_ppm": 1000000000,
    "max_round_tick_cap": 996,
    "doubling_ticks": 100,
    "tick_quantum_ms": 50,
    "crash_point_ppm": "clamp( half_up( HOUSE_EDGE_PPM * 2^64 / (2^64 - raw_u64) ), SCALE_PPM, MAX_MULTIPLIER_CAP_PPM ); i128 intermediate",
    "multiplier_ppm": "m(N) = (1 << (N/100)) * FRACTIONAL_POW2_PPM[N%100], with N first clamped to max_round_tick_cap",
    "crash_tick": "smallest N>=0 with m(N) >= crash_point_ppm, clamped to max_round_tick_cap",
    "rounding": "half-up (midpoint away from zero), mirroring game-engine-core/src/fixed_point.rs",
    "hex_scenarios": "Seeds in the production form: server_seed_hex is 64 lowercase hex chars and the engine's client seed is effective_client_seed_hex = lowercase hex of blake2b-256(client_seed_text) (the client seed is hashed once, at bet time); both hex strings are fed to derive_seed as text. Each entry's server_seed_hex = hex(blake2b-256(b'<name>-<search_index>')), where search_index is the smallest N >= 0 for which the entry's predicate holds"
  },
